<title>UK: ICI shares hit by profit-taking.</title>
<headline>ICI shares hit by profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Chemical Industries Plc fell 24 pence, or 2.83 percent, to 825 on Tuesday as profit-taking ended a recent sprint upwards, analysts said.</p>
<p>ICI had been one of the best performing FTSE 100 stocks after the chemicals group on May 7 announced it would buy Unilever's speciality chemicals business.</p>
<p>The eight billion dollar acquisition was approved by ICI shareholders on Monday after the company's shares hit a 1997 high of 864 pence last week.</p>
<p>The shares had closed at 714-1/2 pence on May 6, the day before the Unilever deal was announced.</p>
<p>&quot;It was time for a correction,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
